  "evidence": "TEXT_F: Protect NHS budget with patient guarantees; maintain police and PCSO numbers with firm action on anti‑social behaviour; points‑based immigration with no unskilled migration from outside the EU and restricted access to benefits; focus on jobs via Future Jobs Fund and mandatory jobs/training; plan to more than halve the deficit by 2014 through growth, fair taxes and efficiencies. TEXT_D: Raise personal allowance to £10,000 and identify savings; scrap ID cards and pass a Freedom Bill; presumption against short prison sentences and cancel mega‑prisons; earned regularisation for long‑resident irregular migrants; oppose new nuclear power and cancel Heathrow third runway.",
  "reasoning": "Voters in 2010 prioritised the economy and jobs, NHS protection, and tougher approaches to crime and immigration, which are more directly reflected in TEXT_F’s commitments to protect NHS funding, maintain police numbers with firm ASB action, restrict non‑EU unskilled migration, and deliver job guarantees while reducing the deficit. TEXT_D places greater emphasis on civil liberties, softer sentencing, and earned regularisation on immigration, which were less aligned with the median electorate’s priorities despite its popular income tax allowance policy.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_F"
}
